WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.601
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.871 --> 00:19.332
All right. Here, right?

3
00:22.460 --> 00:24.587
It's so peaceful here.

4
00:24.671 --> 00:26.923
I feel empty somehow.

5
00:27.006 --> 00:30.468
Things were tough, but it feels sad now that it's over.

6
00:30.552 --> 00:32.971
Stop wallowing and get back to work.

7
00:33.054 --> 00:35.598
Habu, did you finish the door and window plans?

8
00:36.349 --> 00:37.725
Ms. Aso.

9
00:38.852 --> 00:40.186
I miss you.

10
00:40.895 --> 00:43.565
You're wallowing over something else entirely!

11
00:43.648 --> 00:47.193
Wait, you haven't seen Mr. Uramawashi at all since then?

12
00:47.277 --> 00:50.947
He gave his one-sided goodbye, and that was it.

13
00:51.030 --> 00:52.490
Goodbye.

14
00:58.079 --> 01:00.248
That was also a lie, right?

15
01:01.875 --> 01:03.626
-Thank you for waiting. -Thank you.

16
01:03.710 --> 01:06.546
-He moved on fast, didn't he? -It's not just moving on.

17
01:06.629 --> 01:07.922
He's too cold-hearted.

18
01:08.006 --> 01:10.258
-You miss Mr. Uramawashi. -No way!

19
01:10.341 --> 01:11.885
That's not it at all.

20
01:11.968 --> 01:14.679
But since you stopped monitoring Mr. Uramawashi

21
01:14.762 --> 01:16.264
haven't you been a bit down?

22
01:16.347 --> 01:17.724
Well, that's true.

23
01:17.807 --> 01:20.685
I feel out of sorts.

24
01:22.604 --> 01:25.273
It doesn't mean I miss him, though!

25
01:25.982 --> 01:28.610
Still, it's too bad he quit being a lawyer.

26
01:28.693 --> 01:31.237
He's focusing purely on architecture now, right?

27
01:31.321 --> 01:34.449
Ms. Shiramoto's retrial hasn't even started yet.

28
01:36.910 --> 01:39.454
-It's Mr. Uramawashi. -Speak of the devil.

29
01:39.537 --> 01:41.372
He always calls so suddenly.

30
01:42.123 --> 01:42.999
Yes.

31
01:43.833 --> 01:44.792
Aso.

32
01:45.376 --> 01:47.503
Come to the office right now.

33
01:47.587 --> 01:49.881
Huh? Right now?

34
01:50.548 --> 01:52.008
Ms. Aso…

35
01:53.468 --> 01:54.385
It's here!

36
01:56.679 --> 01:57.847
-Oh, right. -Aso?

37
01:57.931 --> 02:00.183
How about some chocolate to liven things up?

38
02:00.266 --> 02:03.019
-Liven things up? You're just playing. -Aso?

39
02:05.355 --> 02:07.732
What do you think? I made it this morning.

40
02:07.815 --> 02:10.193
It feels handmade.

41
02:10.276 --> 02:13.279
Like elementary school Valentine's Day chocolate.

42
02:13.363 --> 02:16.157
It might look like that, but I guarantee the taste is good.

43
02:16.241 --> 02:17.992
-Yeah, it's chocolate… -It's good.

44
02:18.076 --> 02:18.993
Right?

45
02:19.077 --> 02:20.787
Eat up.

46
02:21.454 --> 02:22.914
I'll have some later.

47
02:22.997 --> 02:26.626
I need Mr. Uramawashi to check this interior elevation drawing first.

48
02:27.252 --> 02:28.920
Oh, he's with a client.

49
02:29.003 --> 02:30.255
-A client? -Yes.

50
02:30.338 --> 02:32.340
He wants to become his apprentice.

51
02:33.299 --> 02:34.342
Apprentice?

52
02:36.469 --> 02:41.474
I admire you, and so I, Go Ijuin, became a licensed lawyer!

53
02:41.557 --> 02:44.227
-Make me your apprentice. -Go Ijuin?

54
02:45.144 --> 02:47.647
I feel like I've heard that name before.

55
02:47.730 --> 02:48.898
Despite my looks,

56
02:48.982 --> 02:51.651
I'm super good at telling lies and spotting them,

57
02:51.734 --> 02:53.611
so I'm sure I can be of use.

58
02:53.695 --> 02:55.446
You came here at a bad time.

59
02:56.197 --> 02:59.075
I already retired as a lawyer.

60
03:00.243 --> 03:02.245
What an obvious lie.

61
03:02.328 --> 03:03.705
I see right through it.

62
03:06.833 --> 03:07.917
This…

63
03:08.876 --> 03:10.503
What do you think it is?

64
03:11.087 --> 03:12.171
Chocolate.

65
03:12.255 --> 03:13.631
It looks a bit plain.

66
03:13.715 --> 03:18.928
It is super high-end chocolate from Ginza, 8,000 yen apiece.

67
03:19.554 --> 03:21.514
Seriously, 8,000 yen for this?

68
03:21.597 --> 03:22.682
Try it.

69
03:22.765 --> 03:25.351
May I? Thank you!

70
03:31.441 --> 03:32.692
How is it?

71
03:36.529 --> 03:38.031
It's delicious!

72
03:38.114 --> 03:40.658
8,000 yen chocolate really hits different!

73
03:41.200 --> 03:42.410
You…

74
03:42.493 --> 03:44.662
are not cut out to be a lawyer.

75
03:44.746 --> 03:46.289
Wait a second!

76
03:47.874 --> 03:49.959
Please! Train me!

77
03:50.501 --> 03:52.962
I made this too. Look!

78
03:53.046 --> 03:54.297
URA

79
03:56.132 --> 03:59.552
You're not fit to be a lawyer.

80
04:10.563 --> 04:12.774
-I want some tea… -Hello.

81
04:13.900 --> 04:15.610
Ms. Aso, have some tea.

82
04:15.693 --> 04:16.944
No thanks.

83
04:17.028 --> 04:19.155
Thank you! I was feeling thirsty.

84
04:19.238 --> 04:20.615
This isn't for you.

85
04:20.698 --> 04:23.409
-But she said she didn't want it-- -Excuse me.

86
04:23.910 --> 04:26.120
Mr. Uramawashi left for work.

87
04:26.204 --> 04:28.873
What? He called me here and then left for work?

88
04:28.956 --> 04:32.377
Actually, a client of ours has something they want to consult about.

89
04:32.460 --> 04:33.711
Please help them out.

90
04:33.795 --> 04:34.921
What is it?

91
04:35.546 --> 04:36.798
Wait, are they here?

92
04:36.881 --> 04:39.217
-They're here. -Why? What the heck?

93
04:39.300 --> 04:40.426
-Please. -Why me?

94
04:40.510 --> 04:42.720
-Here you go, Ms. Aso. -Thank you.

95
04:42.804 --> 04:45.681
-Wait a minute! -You're the only one we can ask.

96
04:45.765 --> 04:48.684
It will depend on the details.

97
04:48.768 --> 04:50.978
I think you should go meet with them, Ms. Aso.

98
04:51.062 --> 04:53.523
Why? I haven't said I'll do it yet.

99
04:53.606 --> 04:55.400
-Just talk to-- -No, wait!

100
04:57.276 --> 04:59.362
I haven't said I'll do it yet, okay?

101
04:59.445 --> 05:02.615
Just hear them out. Mrs. Takashima, thank you for waiting.

102
05:02.698 --> 05:04.283
Huh? Runa?

103
05:04.367 --> 05:06.869
So you do know her. She's a popular influencer after all.

104
05:06.953 --> 05:09.122
I always watch your makeup videos!

105
05:09.205 --> 05:12.667
Thank you so much. I apologize for the sudden visit.

106
05:12.750 --> 05:16.337
Honestly, I came to consult with Mr. Uramawashi, but…

107
05:16.421 --> 05:19.632
Unfortunately, he retired. Ms. Aso has taken over for him.

108
05:20.967 --> 05:23.636
For now, let me hear your story.

109
05:25.096 --> 05:27.682
I want to divorce my husband right away!

110
05:27.765 --> 05:30.810
You're about to build your own home together, right?

111
05:30.893 --> 05:32.937
Are you sure about a divorce?

112
05:33.020 --> 05:35.648
I can't stand being with that man anymore!

113
05:35.731 --> 05:38.860
Could you tell me what happened?

114
05:41.028 --> 05:45.199
I got scammed at a beauty salon.

115
05:45.283 --> 05:46.826
Scammed?

116
05:46.909 --> 05:48.119
This one.

117
05:49.620 --> 05:50.830
TRIAL 500 YEN

118
05:50.913 --> 05:52.498
This person…

119
05:52.582 --> 05:54.584
The celebrity Ayako Katsuta?

120
05:54.667 --> 05:57.628
Lately, it seems she started running a beauty salon.

121
05:58.212 --> 06:01.257
I got a message from the salon inviting me for a trial.

122
06:01.340 --> 06:04.927
The price was 500 yen, which seemed cheap, so I gave it a try.

123
06:07.555 --> 06:10.391
Mrs. Takashima, thank you for completing the trial.

124
06:10.474 --> 06:11.851
How was it?

125
06:12.476 --> 06:15.104
I feel like it went pretty well.

126
06:15.188 --> 06:16.689
-Glad to hear that. -Yes.

127
06:16.772 --> 06:18.232
Hello.

128
06:18.316 --> 06:19.775
Huh? For real?

129
06:19.859 --> 06:22.653
Thank you for coming today.

130
06:22.737 --> 06:26.449
This is our recommended plan for you.

131
06:26.532 --> 06:29.202
Huh? It costs a million yen?

132
06:29.285 --> 06:33.372
Actually, if you sign the contract on this trial day,

133
06:34.165 --> 06:35.917
it only costs 600,000 yen.

134
06:36.000 --> 06:38.127
It really gets that cheap?

135
06:38.211 --> 06:40.922
You get the best deal if you start today!

136
06:41.005 --> 06:45.343
As a special offer, we'll also give you a complimentary beauty serum.

137
06:45.927 --> 06:47.470
Then I'll sign.

138
06:47.553 --> 06:49.597
Please sign here.

139
06:59.565 --> 07:02.568
But, I've only been able to do one session.

140
07:02.652 --> 07:04.153
What do you mean?

141
07:04.237 --> 07:08.115
They won't let her make a reservation, citing that they are fully booked.

142
07:08.199 --> 07:11.410
I lied to my husband, saying it was a proper salon,

143
07:11.494 --> 07:12.495
but he found out.

144
07:12.578 --> 07:14.413
They then had a huge fight.

145
07:14.997 --> 07:19.126
But he also lied about having work so he could fool around before.

146
07:19.210 --> 07:22.630
-Why do I get yelled at, and not him? -I understand.

147
07:22.713 --> 07:25.591
First, why don't we solve the salon issue?

148
07:26.217 --> 07:27.885
Can we really do that?

149
07:27.969 --> 07:30.846
I'll look into the reason why you can't make a reservation.

150
07:30.930 --> 07:33.599
Salons are under the Commercial Transactions Act,

151
07:33.683 --> 07:35.935
so you can cancel and demand a refund.

152
07:36.018 --> 07:37.812
I can get my money back?

153
07:37.895 --> 07:40.856
Just to be sure, could you bring the contract next time?

154
07:40.940 --> 07:43.526
I think deciding on a divorce can wait until after.

155
07:43.609 --> 07:44.944
I understand.

156
07:45.027 --> 07:46.487
Thanks for your help.

157
07:53.911 --> 07:56.038
Ms. Aso, I bought some ice cream…

158
07:56.122 --> 07:57.623
She just left.

159
07:58.207 --> 08:00.084
-Huh? -Too bad.

160
08:00.167 --> 08:01.252
What?

161
08:01.836 --> 08:03.713
-Jeez. -I want strawberry.

162
08:03.796 --> 08:04.630
I want matcha.

163
08:04.714 --> 08:07.258
You have no chance. Why don't you give up?

164
08:07.341 --> 08:10.469
If I gave up over this, I might as well not try at all!

165
08:10.553 --> 08:12.346
Don't yell at us like that.

166
08:12.930 --> 08:17.101
That's how much I like Ms. Aso.

167
08:18.603 --> 08:20.229
Up until now,

168
08:21.063 --> 08:24.900
the two of us have made so many memories together.

169
08:35.244 --> 08:37.788
-I've met you-- -Why have you come to see him?

170
08:37.872 --> 08:39.832
-I will guide you. -No need.

171
08:41.000 --> 08:44.086
Good morning, Ms. Aso. You look lovely today too.

172
08:45.046 --> 08:46.047
Thank you very much.

173
08:46.130 --> 08:47.882
-Do you have a boyfriend? -Shut up.

174
08:48.966 --> 08:50.676
I've watched over her.

175
08:50.760 --> 08:53.262
SCHOOL ROUTE ITABASHI WARD

176
08:56.390 --> 08:57.808
He's so staying overnight.

177
08:57.892 --> 09:00.186
-Be quiet for a bit! -Sure.

178
09:00.269 --> 09:03.731
-Watched over her? -That's just stalker behavior.

179
09:03.814 --> 09:05.483
I bought her refreshments too.

180
09:05.566 --> 09:07.360
I bought it for you. Here you go!

181
09:07.443 --> 09:09.153
I don't do sugar this early.

182
09:09.236 --> 09:10.905
Here, please use this.

183
09:13.449 --> 09:15.493
I've fought against rivals too.

184
09:17.119 --> 09:19.830
It wasn't even a competition though.

185
09:19.914 --> 09:22.500
-You were peeping? -Things were tough, but…

186
09:22.583 --> 09:24.085
The name is cut off midway.

187
09:24.168 --> 09:25.670
But I overcame them.

188
09:27.546 --> 09:29.507
Those were all really trivial moments.

189
09:29.590 --> 09:31.217
-It's memory bias. -That's it.

190
09:32.259 --> 09:34.970
I wonder if Mrs. Takashima and her husband can make up?

191
09:35.054 --> 09:36.972
They have to, or we're in trouble.

192
09:37.056 --> 09:39.684
The permits are approved, construction is a go!

193
09:39.767 --> 09:41.852
If they get a divorce,

194
09:41.936 --> 09:44.438
our work on their home will be canceled, right?

195
09:44.522 --> 09:47.525
We can't let that happen! All our efforts will go down the drain!

196
09:47.608 --> 09:49.652
It will put us in the red.

197
09:49.735 --> 09:52.613
To be honest, our finances are pretty bad.

198
09:52.697 --> 09:55.116
-Will we go bankrupt? -Hey, don't jinx us!

199
09:55.199 --> 09:58.077
So that all of us don't end up on the streets,

200
09:58.160 --> 09:59.495
let's get to it.

201
09:59.578 --> 10:00.496
To what?

202
10:00.579 --> 10:02.957
For now, I'll look into Katsuta.

203
10:03.040 --> 10:04.959
I made a reservation for the trial plan.

204
10:05.042 --> 10:07.086
I'll go there tomorrow.

205
10:08.045 --> 10:09.880
No!

206
10:10.631 --> 10:12.508
No!

207
10:13.008 --> 10:15.511
Last time, you said it was the last time!

208
10:15.594 --> 10:16.721
I…

209
10:16.804 --> 10:18.180
won't be participating!

210
10:19.098 --> 10:21.100
Don't yell like that.

211
10:21.183 --> 10:23.519
-You're going to do it, Sabayama. -Let's do it.

212
10:23.602 --> 10:24.854
I won't!

213
10:24.937 --> 10:26.731
I definitely won't!

214
10:26.814 --> 10:28.232
No way in hell!

215
10:33.487 --> 10:34.989
Welcome.

216
10:35.072 --> 10:37.158
I'm Aso, a lawyer.

217
10:37.241 --> 10:39.952
I would like to speak with Ms. Katsuta, your CEO.

218
10:40.035 --> 10:42.747
I'll go check. Please wait a moment.

219
10:46.375 --> 10:49.128
Next is the counseling session. This way, please.

220
10:49.211 --> 10:51.756
-You offer counseling sessions? -Yes.

221
10:51.839 --> 10:55.050
And just for 500 yen? It's incredibly cheap.

222
10:55.134 --> 10:56.719
Thank you very much.

223
11:00.222 --> 11:01.640
I'm Hikawa, her secretary.

224
11:01.724 --> 11:03.017
I'm Aso, an attorney.

225
11:03.100 --> 11:05.770
I'm very sorry, but Ms. Katsuta is in a meeting.

226
11:06.353 --> 11:07.605
I see.

227
11:07.688 --> 11:10.649
Can you please show me your reservation calendar?

228
11:12.485 --> 11:13.402
Yes.

229
11:22.286 --> 11:23.537
Here it is.

230
11:25.372 --> 11:29.960
RESERVATION CALENDAR

231
11:30.044 --> 11:32.630
It's booked quite far in advance.

232
11:33.130 --> 11:36.884
Doesn't the difficulty in booking contradict customer expectations?

233
11:36.967 --> 11:40.971
About that, we are currently limiting the number of new customers,

234
11:41.055 --> 11:44.016
so that there will be open reservation slots.

235
11:48.562 --> 11:50.731
Sales of the beauty serum are going well.

236
11:50.814 --> 11:53.984
We got lots of bookings for the trial plan today too.

237
11:54.068 --> 11:57.821
The lawyer from earlier checked the reservation calendar and left.

238
11:58.489 --> 12:00.824
You showed them the usual one, right?

239
12:01.492 --> 12:02.326
Yes.

240
12:04.954 --> 12:08.624
Should we not be worried with a lawyer poking around?

241
12:09.416 --> 12:11.627
If they want to investigate, let them.

242
12:12.211 --> 12:16.507
We didn't force anyone into a contract, and we do provide treatments.

243
12:17.383 --> 12:18.384
Yes, ma'am.

244
12:20.135 --> 12:22.596
We haven't done anything wrong.

245
12:23.180 --> 12:25.558
So hurry up and get more contracts.

246
12:26.600 --> 12:27.810
Yes, ma'am!

247
12:30.437 --> 12:34.441
When I tried to reserve the trial plan Habu went to,

248
12:35.734 --> 12:38.571
I could book anytime, like this.

249
12:39.321 --> 12:40.739
It's not fully booked at all.

250
12:40.823 --> 12:44.535
Maybe once you become a member, reservations get restricted.

251
12:45.202 --> 12:47.621
They hold monthly talk shows at the salon,

252
12:47.705 --> 12:50.082
and it seems you can try their services too.

253
12:50.165 --> 12:52.793
Using her fame to gather lots of people all at once.

254
12:52.876 --> 12:53.919
On social media,

255
12:54.003 --> 12:56.755
I found people in the same situation as Mrs. Takashima.

256
12:56.839 --> 12:58.799
They can't make reservations.

257
12:58.882 --> 13:01.135
-I'm back. -You're late!

258
13:01.218 --> 13:03.554
Don't tell me you took a detour?

259
13:03.637 --> 13:05.848
I was just asking the staff various things.

260
13:05.931 --> 13:07.224
Did you find out anything?

261
13:07.308 --> 13:10.686
For now, I got the contract form the salon uses.

262
13:15.441 --> 13:16.358
You…

263
13:16.442 --> 13:17.651
Don't tell me you…

264
13:17.735 --> 13:18.777
I signed it.

265
13:18.861 --> 13:20.613
You got played like a total sucker!

266
13:20.696 --> 13:21.780
Why did you go there?

267
13:21.864 --> 13:24.116
I found their explanation to be reasonable.

268
13:24.199 --> 13:26.910
Oh, it's already posted on the salon's social media.

269
13:26.994 --> 13:29.496
TODAY'S CUSTOMER HE SIGNED UP FOR OUR RECOMMENDED PLAN!

270
13:29.580 --> 13:33.208
You couldn't refuse this pretty lady.

271
13:33.292 --> 13:34.710
You cheater!

272
13:34.793 --> 13:37.546
No, wait. It wasn't like that.

273
13:37.630 --> 13:40.174
-You're grinning like an idiot. -Am I?

274
13:40.758 --> 13:42.426
This is the contract.

275
13:45.179 --> 13:49.224
If you sign up at the campaign price on the trial day,

276
13:49.308 --> 13:54.813
you cannot cancel for the first year, and you also cannot get a refund.

277
13:56.023 --> 13:59.276
Since it says that, I thought I couldn't cancel.

278
13:59.985 --> 14:02.071
Under the Commercial Transactions Act,

279
14:02.154 --> 14:05.282
this sentence shouldn't prevent you from canceling.

280
14:05.991 --> 14:07.076
Huh?

281
14:07.159 --> 14:08.911
Is this a business contract?

282
14:08.994 --> 14:11.497
Yes. I am a solo entrepreneur.

283
14:11.580 --> 14:14.750
They told me I could write it off as a tax-deductible expense.

284
14:17.670 --> 14:18.921
Hello.

285
14:19.004 --> 14:20.589
Oh, Ms. Aso, what's up?

286
14:21.173 --> 14:24.009
I have to speak with Mrs. Takashima's husband.

287
14:24.093 --> 14:25.552
Oh, I see.

288
14:25.636 --> 14:27.471
I'm working overtime.

289
14:27.554 --> 14:30.516
Because Mr. Uramawashi is slacking off.

290
14:30.599 --> 14:34.103
Mr. Kureta, you've known Mr. Uramawashi for a long time, right?

291
14:34.186 --> 14:38.148
We met after graduating from university, so it has been over 20 years.

292
14:38.232 --> 14:40.317
Don't you ever get fed up?

293
14:40.401 --> 14:42.569
He's selfish and tells nothing but lies.

294
14:43.153 --> 14:46.365
Well, all of that makes Mr. Uramawashi who he is.

295
14:46.448 --> 14:47.783
You're so kind.

296
14:49.326 --> 14:52.663
For buildings, you know, their appearance is important,

297
14:52.746 --> 14:56.500
but I think how the inside is constructed is even more important.

298
14:57.126 --> 14:59.962
Maybe humans are the same.

299
15:03.757 --> 15:06.218
Bye. I have a date.

300
15:06.301 --> 15:09.179
-Huh? -I'm treating my daughter to BBQ.

301
15:17.604 --> 15:21.900
My wife suddenly told me she might have been scammed,

302
15:21.984 --> 15:24.611
so I panicked, and my mind went blank.

303
15:24.695 --> 15:28.032
And so without thinking, you ended up blaming her.

304
15:29.324 --> 15:31.577
I mean, it's 600,000 yen!

305
15:32.202 --> 15:36.874
Just when we've been saving up and working hard for our dream home.

306
15:36.957 --> 15:39.585
It hasn't been proven that it's a scam yet.

307
15:39.668 --> 15:44.882
We kept fighting, so we had to stop the meetings for the house.

308
15:46.091 --> 15:48.677
I don't think we can make it work anymore.

309
15:52.139 --> 15:55.309
This is the original copy of Mrs. Takashima's contract.

310
15:55.392 --> 15:56.894
May I take a photo of this?

311
15:56.977 --> 15:58.062
Go ahead.

312
16:05.069 --> 16:07.738
May I meet with Ms. Katsuta?

313
16:08.238 --> 16:09.698
She is…

314
16:09.782 --> 16:11.825
Such a young lawyer, I see.

315
16:12.326 --> 16:14.495
I'm Aso, representing Mrs. Takashima.

316
16:14.578 --> 16:17.873
I apologize for the difficulty in making reservations.

317
16:17.956 --> 16:20.709
When the situation improves, she can come for treatments.

318
16:21.543 --> 16:24.046
But no one knows when that will be.

319
16:28.717 --> 16:31.804
The contract. You've read it, right?

320
16:33.472 --> 16:36.141
Mrs. Takashima signed it after reading it through,

321
16:36.225 --> 16:37.935
with full understanding.

322
16:40.145 --> 16:43.482
I've handled divorce trials for various couples.

323
16:44.233 --> 16:49.279
It's not why you fought, but the broken trust that's the real issue.

324
16:49.863 --> 16:52.658
I don't think either of them really wants a divorce.

325
16:52.741 --> 16:54.201
I have to do something.

326
16:54.284 --> 16:55.577
You think you can do it?

327
16:55.661 --> 16:57.079
Well…

328
16:57.162 --> 17:00.124
It won't be easy.

329
17:00.707 --> 17:02.292
You can do it!

330
17:02.376 --> 17:06.255
I mean, you've gone through Mr. Uramawashi's training, right?

331
17:08.674 --> 17:10.425
I got tired of being a lawyer.

332
17:10.509 --> 17:11.802
-What? -That's a lie.

333
17:11.885 --> 17:13.178
What?!

334
17:13.262 --> 17:14.304
Please wait.

335
17:14.388 --> 17:16.431
Please wait!

336
17:16.932 --> 17:18.600
Are you a rabbit?

337
17:18.684 --> 17:20.310
You must be scared.

338
17:20.394 --> 17:21.854
I'm not scared!

339
17:21.937 --> 17:22.855
Then, take it on.

340
17:22.938 --> 17:24.064
No way.

341
17:24.815 --> 17:29.278
It wasn't training, more like him dragging me into things.

342
17:29.361 --> 17:33.699
You have decided that lies are black-hearted things.

343
17:34.491 --> 17:37.494
However, reality isn't painted in such simple colors.

344
17:37.578 --> 17:39.872
Fight poison with poison.

345
17:39.955 --> 17:41.999
There are times when that is necessary.

346
17:42.082 --> 17:45.794
The one who protected Yazu was you, Aso.

347
17:46.837 --> 17:48.213
Thank you, woof!

348
17:48.297 --> 17:52.759
From now on, you can fight fair and square,

349
17:52.843 --> 17:55.137
your own way.

350
17:56.972 --> 18:00.976
But you really have changed in a good way.

351
18:01.059 --> 18:02.895
-Do you think so? -Yeah!

352
18:02.978 --> 18:05.189
I'm so proud of you as your senior.

353
18:07.691 --> 18:10.360
Thank you very much. It's all thanks to you!

354
18:10.986 --> 18:13.155
All right, do your best.

355
18:13.238 --> 18:14.281
Yes.

356
18:21.538 --> 18:24.291
There must be an opening somewhere!

357
18:37.930 --> 18:40.515
To think this day would actually come.

358
18:41.600 --> 18:45.479
It's truly thanks to all of you.

359
18:46.355 --> 18:50.442
About the retrial, Ms. Aso is making sure it proceeds smoothly.

360
18:51.151 --> 18:52.861
I'm not worried at all.

361
18:55.697 --> 18:56.698
Ms. Shiramoto.

362
18:57.574 --> 18:58.533
Yes.

363
18:59.159 --> 19:00.327
Ten years ago,

364
19:00.994 --> 19:03.288
I couldn't defend you.

365
19:04.039 --> 19:05.040
I'm sorry.

366
19:05.123 --> 19:07.751
I should be the one apologizing!

367
19:07.834 --> 19:11.505
Mr. Moriki, you were worried and warned me, but I…

368
19:12.047 --> 19:13.674
I'm so sorry.

369
19:14.841 --> 19:16.426
Once the retrial is over,

370
19:16.510 --> 19:21.598
I'll do my best to help you return to being a lawyer.

371
19:22.891 --> 19:23.976
May I?

372
19:24.518 --> 19:27.562
I want you to personally train Aso.

373
19:29.231 --> 19:32.859
I will do my best not to let you down.

374
19:35.028 --> 19:36.071
Also,

375
19:37.197 --> 19:38.490
one more thing.

376
19:38.573 --> 19:39.574
Yes.

377
19:40.367 --> 19:41.493
Actually,

378
19:42.995 --> 19:44.037
it's about Uramawashi.

379
19:44.121 --> 19:45.455
Did he quit being a lawyer?

380
19:46.748 --> 19:48.458
I had a feeling he did.

381
19:48.542 --> 19:49.876
Amazing.

382
19:50.460 --> 19:51.420
You guessed it.

383
19:52.087 --> 19:53.255
That's a relief.

384
19:53.797 --> 19:56.883
I mean, my big brother isn't cut out to be a lawyer.

385
19:56.967 --> 19:58.302
-That's true. -Yes.

386
20:05.684 --> 20:06.893
Look here.

387
20:07.519 --> 20:08.353
Here.

388
20:08.437 --> 20:10.522
There's a mark from a pen test scribble.

389
20:10.605 --> 20:13.025
I always do that out of habit.

390
20:13.108 --> 20:18.071
And this is the copy of your contract, which I got from the salon.

391
20:18.155 --> 20:20.532
CONTRACT

392
20:20.615 --> 20:22.326
There's no test scribble!

393
20:22.826 --> 20:24.161
I think…

394
20:24.244 --> 20:26.872
Between the first page, which you saw during signing,

395
20:26.955 --> 20:30.250
and the second page that you signed, the text was altered.

396
20:30.334 --> 20:31.585
Huh?

397
20:32.794 --> 20:36.631
They show favorable terms to the customer to get them to sign,

398
20:36.715 --> 20:40.093
but include unfavorable terms in the customer's copy.

399
20:40.177 --> 20:43.305
This original copy might have been fabricated in case

400
20:43.388 --> 20:45.432
someone requested disclosure.

401
20:46.808 --> 20:49.436
If we pursue this possibility of falsification,

402
20:49.519 --> 20:51.897
I think we can demand a refund.

403
20:54.524 --> 20:55.901
But there's no need.

404
20:56.526 --> 20:57.361
Huh?

405
20:57.444 --> 21:00.822
We fought again this morning, and I'm just tired of it.

406
21:01.448 --> 21:04.201
Screw the money! I just want to get divorced.

407
21:08.538 --> 21:09.873
I think this should be fine.

408
21:09.956 --> 21:11.083
Here you go.

409
21:11.166 --> 21:14.419
Once they get stubborn, things only get messier.

410
21:14.503 --> 21:17.005
Sometimes, it hurts less to just get it over with.

411
21:17.089 --> 21:18.048
He's been through it.

412
21:18.131 --> 21:19.841
-Shut up! -Sorry.

413
21:21.927 --> 21:26.390
I was so close to solving the salon case!

414
21:30.644 --> 21:32.687
We have a rare guest.

415
21:32.771 --> 21:35.065
Mr. Fujiwara! It has been a while.

416
21:35.148 --> 21:37.025
Long time no see.

417
21:37.109 --> 21:39.111
You all look as energetic as ever.

418
21:39.694 --> 21:41.780
We built a house for him in the past.

419
21:41.863 --> 21:44.157
He is a famous lawyer from Osaka!

420
21:44.241 --> 21:46.368
We bumped into each other outside.

421
21:46.451 --> 21:49.079
He said he wanted to thank you all again.

422
21:50.414 --> 21:54.167
Thank you so much for the wonderful house.

423
21:54.876 --> 21:58.213
Back when we were building it, my wife and I rarely agreed,

424
21:58.296 --> 21:59.840
so we were always fighting.

425
21:59.923 --> 22:01.925
Sorry for all that trouble!

426
22:02.008 --> 22:03.385
-I remember that. -Yes.

427
22:03.468 --> 22:07.222
Your wife insisted on building a dedicated takoyaki maker in the kitchen.

428
22:07.305 --> 22:08.849
How nostalgic.

429
22:08.932 --> 22:11.184
-I remember your wife was really tall. -Yes.

430
22:11.268 --> 22:13.854
You almost got divorced over takoyaki.

431
22:13.937 --> 22:15.188
No.

432
22:15.272 --> 22:17.065
To be honest with you now,

433
22:17.649 --> 22:20.485
that was actually my fault.

434
22:21.695 --> 22:24.072
My wife said she liked takoyaki,

435
22:24.156 --> 22:27.325
so I said I loved takoyaki too, just to go along with her.

436
22:27.409 --> 22:29.202
I ended up telling a lie.

437
22:29.286 --> 22:32.789
So that's why your wife was so insistent on takoyaki.

438
22:32.873 --> 22:36.710
Then when I said a built-in takoyaki maker would be in the way,

439
22:36.793 --> 22:38.670
we had a massive fight.

440
22:38.753 --> 22:41.798
-I'm just glad you didn't get divorced. -No, but…

441
22:41.882 --> 22:43.675
Thanks to building the house,

442
22:43.758 --> 22:46.803
we've gotten better at both fighting and making up.

443
22:49.431 --> 22:51.141
I almost forgot to tell you.

444
22:51.766 --> 22:55.020
I brought a takoyaki-making set as thanks.

445
22:55.604 --> 22:58.148
Let's all have a takoyaki party!

446
22:58.231 --> 22:59.858
-Look! -So nice.

447
22:59.941 --> 23:02.485
-Amazing. -How about this?

448
23:02.569 --> 23:04.779
With this, let's make some takoyaki.

449
23:04.863 --> 23:07.115
Cute, right?

450
23:31.806 --> 23:35.060
Ayako Katsuta agreed to an interview.

451
23:44.152 --> 23:47.822
This is a drawing of lies and truth.

452
23:49.783 --> 23:51.993
-Good morning. -Morning.

453
23:52.077 --> 23:53.662
I have a favor to ask.

454
23:53.745 --> 23:56.206
-Huh? Where is everyone? -Running an errand.

455
23:57.207 --> 23:58.792
Huh…

456
23:59.709 --> 24:01.753
Is your favor by any chance this?

457
24:02.629 --> 24:06.299
The design of the Takashima couple's new house.

458
24:06.383 --> 24:08.843
Did you know I was coming to pick it up?

459
24:09.594 --> 24:11.054
Mr. Uramawashi did.

460
24:18.770 --> 24:20.939
I said I wouldn't do this anymore.

461
24:21.022 --> 24:22.691
You look great in that outfit.

462
24:22.774 --> 24:24.776
-Really? -Better than your normal clothes.

463
24:24.859 --> 24:26.987
-Looking cool. -Don't say that!

464
24:27.070 --> 24:29.489
-I'm an architect. -Sorry for the wait.

465
24:34.661 --> 24:36.788
Shall we go then?

466
24:38.123 --> 24:39.833
-All of us have glasses. -What?

467
24:39.916 --> 24:41.793
Mr. Kureta, those glasses…

468
24:42.294 --> 24:44.587
They are so lame!

469
24:44.671 --> 24:46.339
-A bit. -Really?

470
24:46.423 --> 24:47.257
TAKASHIMA HOUSE PLANS

471
24:55.515 --> 24:57.350
This lighting is really great.

472
24:57.434 --> 25:00.353
It's not about being great. How much did this cost?

473
25:00.437 --> 25:02.230
Isn't this a bit too much?

474
25:02.314 --> 25:03.523
We can write it off, no?

475
25:03.606 --> 25:05.150
Write it off…

476
25:05.692 --> 25:06.943
Ms. Katsuta.

477
25:07.027 --> 25:09.070
Thank you for your time today.

478
25:09.154 --> 25:11.531
I'm so happy to be on TV!

479
25:11.614 --> 25:12.782
Please, this way.

480
25:13.408 --> 25:16.161
Ms. Katsuta, not only are you a talented entrepreneur,

481
25:16.244 --> 25:18.204
you're also really beautiful.

482
25:18.288 --> 25:20.040
It's all thanks to our salon.

483
25:20.123 --> 25:22.459
Must be nice. I want to try it too.

484
25:22.542 --> 25:25.295
We have affordable trial plans. Please give it a try.

485
25:25.378 --> 25:27.088
Thank you very much.

486
25:27.797 --> 25:30.717
When a customer calls for a trial plan,

487
25:30.800 --> 25:33.845
make sure to ask for their preferred dates and make the booking, okay?

488
25:33.928 --> 25:35.096
Yes.

489
25:35.180 --> 25:36.639
-Do your best. -Yes!

490
25:38.266 --> 25:40.560
I understand. I'll do my best.

491
25:41.811 --> 25:42.812
Welcome.

492
25:46.274 --> 25:49.652
So could you tell us about your vision for the future?

493
25:50.320 --> 25:51.363
Right now, I…

494
25:51.446 --> 25:53.782
-Ms. Hikawa, please come with me. -What's wrong?

495
25:53.865 --> 25:56.910
A customer who signed a contract came to complain.

496
25:56.993 --> 25:59.537
Right when we have an interview!

497
26:00.163 --> 26:03.625
You really seem like a true ally to women.

498
26:03.708 --> 26:05.293
-Are you listening? -Yes.

499
26:05.377 --> 26:08.004
I called every day, but I wasn't able to make a booking!

500
26:08.088 --> 26:09.672
-I'm sorry. -What's going on?

501
26:09.756 --> 26:11.633
I'm sorry, I'm a temp--

502
26:11.716 --> 26:13.927
Sir, please calm down.

503
26:14.010 --> 26:16.930
I'm not going to calm down! Explain this to me!

504
26:17.013 --> 26:19.057
It sounds a bit noisy in the lobby.

505
26:19.140 --> 26:21.559
No, I don't hear anything.

506
26:22.268 --> 26:23.686
-You hear anything? -No.

507
26:23.770 --> 26:24.979
I must be imagining it.

508
26:25.063 --> 26:26.564
Let me cancel right now!

509
26:26.648 --> 26:31.403
Customers who joined from the trial plan cannot cancel for the first year.

510
26:31.486 --> 26:33.196
It is clearly stated in the contract.

511
26:33.279 --> 26:34.864
I never knew that.

512
26:34.948 --> 26:36.741
Show me the original contract!

513
26:38.535 --> 26:39.577
Well…

514
26:40.412 --> 26:43.206
You can't show it? Then isn't this a scam?

515
26:43.289 --> 26:44.290
Scam?

516
26:44.874 --> 26:47.335
I understand. Please wait a moment.

517
26:47.919 --> 26:50.088
-Hurry it up! -Yes.

518
26:50.171 --> 26:52.090
Oh, please don't be mad…

519
26:53.883 --> 26:54.843
Ms. Hikawa.

520
26:55.635 --> 26:58.304
I'm sorry. I haven't remade the contract yet.

521
26:59.472 --> 27:00.723
Fine.

522
27:00.807 --> 27:03.059
-I'll do it. -I'm sorry.

523
27:06.438 --> 27:07.272
Nakaza.

524
27:07.856 --> 27:08.898
Now.

525
27:10.442 --> 27:12.277
Oh, it hurts!

526
27:12.360 --> 27:13.778
Hey, are you okay?

527
27:13.862 --> 27:15.155
I'm fine!

528
27:17.615 --> 27:20.410
I'm going to the bathroom. Sorry!

529
27:21.536 --> 27:23.329
Sorry.

530
27:28.585 --> 27:31.671
CANNOT CANCEL DURING FIRST YEAR

531
27:45.768 --> 27:46.644
All right.

532
27:55.195 --> 27:56.988
Ms. Ueno!

533
27:57.071 --> 28:01.075
Earlier, some customers called, and I made a few reservations.

534
28:01.159 --> 28:02.785
-Thank you. -Yes.

535
28:03.828 --> 28:06.998
Huh? These are not for the trial plan.

536
28:07.081 --> 28:09.584
I booked spots for people who already signed with us.

537
28:09.667 --> 28:12.795
I told you to make reservations for the trial plan.

538
28:12.879 --> 28:14.464
-The reservations… -Huh?

539
28:15.632 --> 28:17.759
Only first-time customers get reservations!

540
28:17.842 --> 28:18.885
Only first-timers?

541
28:18.968 --> 28:21.804
Now Ms. Katsuta will be mad at me!

542
28:22.388 --> 28:24.015
I'm sorry.

543
28:25.683 --> 28:27.519
-Oh no. -Nakaza.

544
28:27.602 --> 28:29.270
Calm down.

545
28:29.354 --> 28:31.356
Hide in the back room.

546
28:31.439 --> 28:32.982
The back room?

547
28:35.235 --> 28:37.070
The back room.

548
29:00.927 --> 29:02.762
Of course no one's here.

549
29:10.854 --> 29:13.690
Mr. Uramawashi. Thank you.

550
29:15.108 --> 29:17.527
Sorry. I'll check your entry permit.

551
29:17.610 --> 29:20.113
Huh? We never needed anything like that.

552
29:20.196 --> 29:22.657
-New rules, starting today. -But we are in a hurry.

553
29:22.740 --> 29:25.118
No! It's the rule.

554
29:25.201 --> 29:26.578
-Sorry. -What do you mean?

555
29:26.661 --> 29:27.579
No!

556
29:30.331 --> 29:32.792
Are you satisfied now?

557
29:33.293 --> 29:36.754
No, wait a moment. I'll read it again.

558
29:40.717 --> 29:43.344
Hello. I came for equipment maintenance.

559
29:43.428 --> 29:44.596
Please go ahead.

560
29:45.179 --> 29:46.848
You aren't the usual person.

561
29:46.931 --> 29:49.434
Traffic is a bit congested. They'll join later.

562
29:49.517 --> 29:51.644
The customer earlier said the same.

563
29:52.395 --> 29:53.313
Go ahead.

564
29:53.396 --> 29:54.689
-Excuse me. -Thank you.

565
29:55.565 --> 29:57.442
It's the rule! You can't enter!

566
29:57.525 --> 30:00.778
-No, you really can't. -Don't push us!

567
30:00.862 --> 30:02.614
-Hey, what are you… -You can't!

568
30:02.697 --> 30:04.908
It's the rule. I'm sorry. Boss, hurry!

569
30:05.783 --> 30:07.118
Got it.

570
30:09.579 --> 30:11.205
I came for maintenance.

571
30:11.289 --> 30:12.874
Oh, was it today?

572
30:12.957 --> 30:14.751
Did you forget?

573
30:14.834 --> 30:17.921
-It's today. -Sorry, uh… I got lost.

574
30:18.004 --> 30:20.214
-Oh, I'll guide you. -Is that okay?

575
30:20.298 --> 30:21.341
-Thank you. -Go ahead.

576
30:21.424 --> 30:22.258
Okay.

577
30:22.342 --> 30:24.177
This place is like a maze!

578
30:24.260 --> 30:25.386
It's this way.

579
30:34.228 --> 30:36.397
Thank you so much for today.

580
30:36.481 --> 30:39.150
-Thank you. -Looking forward to the broadcast.

581
30:39.943 --> 30:41.277
Well then, excuse us.

582
30:41.361 --> 30:42.904
-Bye. -Excuse us.

583
30:50.328 --> 30:51.371
Goodbye.

584
30:51.955 --> 30:54.916
-Goodbye, sir. -Fine. I get it.

585
30:54.999 --> 30:56.751
Please come again.

586
30:57.919 --> 31:00.505
Sorry. I have to go too.

587
31:00.588 --> 31:02.048
Excuse me.

588
31:02.131 --> 31:03.883
Bye!

589
31:03.967 --> 31:05.051
What?

590
31:05.843 --> 31:07.804
What's her deal?

591
31:14.852 --> 31:18.147
WHAT DO YOU WANT FROM YOUR NEW HOME?

592
31:33.371 --> 31:35.915
Boss! Why are you slacking off?

593
31:35.999 --> 31:38.126
Hey, that stuff was tiring!

594
31:38.209 --> 31:40.878
Don't "hey" me. Please get back to work.

595
31:40.962 --> 31:43.673
Right. Let's watch some horse racing.

596
31:43.756 --> 31:46.092
Don't watch horse racing!

597
31:46.801 --> 31:50.805
Well, from my side, the project I was in charge of…

598
31:50.888 --> 31:52.473
is also the future of Japan.

599
31:52.557 --> 31:54.767
Yes, I mean the resort project.

600
31:55.727 --> 32:00.148
It will improve Japan's tourism, employment, and economy.

601
32:00.231 --> 32:02.525
It's like he is invulnerable.

602
32:02.608 --> 32:04.902
He's just pretending.

603
32:04.986 --> 32:08.531
His approval rating is dropping, and he's taking a lot of flak.

604
32:09.115 --> 32:11.659
Even so, he refuses to give up, huh.

605
32:11.743 --> 32:13.828
Why is he so determined?

606
32:13.911 --> 32:16.039
I think he didn't act out of self-interest.

607
32:16.122 --> 32:18.374
He was genuinely thinking about the country.

608
32:18.458 --> 32:21.085
I will definitely make it happen.

609
32:21.169 --> 32:26.090
Surprisingly, I think the one most hurt over Mr. Nitou's death might be him.

610
32:26.174 --> 32:29.844
We had our own brand of justice, and I think he had his own.

611
32:29.927 --> 32:32.346
Something he couldn't compromise on.

612
32:34.807 --> 32:36.684
Were we on the side of justice?

613
32:36.768 --> 32:39.270
I believed we were heroes of justice!

614
32:39.353 --> 32:40.313
No, no way!

615
32:40.396 --> 32:43.024
We are at best morally gray! Or even pitch black!

616
32:43.608 --> 32:46.569
Just be glad we could be of help to Mr. Uramawashi.

617
32:46.652 --> 32:49.322
Consider it payback for what he has done for us.

618
32:49.405 --> 32:51.574
Yeah. You're right.

619
32:51.657 --> 32:53.659
Well, shall we get to it then?

620
32:53.743 --> 32:54.994
It's our final job.

621
32:55.078 --> 32:57.080
Before that, should we eat?

622
32:57.163 --> 32:58.706
Thanks for the food.

623
32:58.790 --> 32:59.874
Let's eat.

624
33:00.458 --> 33:01.542
Hey.

625
33:03.628 --> 33:05.088
Is Uramawashi here?

626
33:07.757 --> 33:10.343
Y-Yoshiki?

627
33:10.426 --> 33:11.928
Is it actually him?

628
33:12.011 --> 33:14.722
-It is really him! -He actually came here.

629
33:14.806 --> 33:16.849
-Huh? -His cube is red.

630
33:17.558 --> 33:19.852
Yo, long time no see.

631
33:27.735 --> 33:28.736
Yeah.

632
33:34.867 --> 33:37.578
Yeah.

633
33:41.541 --> 33:43.167
Shall we?

634
33:48.422 --> 33:50.341
Are they the same type?

635
33:50.424 --> 33:53.469
-Were they conversing? -Yeah.

636
33:53.553 --> 33:55.054
Right?

637
34:01.435 --> 34:04.021
Now then, let's have her come on stage.

638
34:04.105 --> 34:07.650
Representing Angewel, Ms. Ayako Katsuta.

639
34:17.660 --> 34:19.745
Hello, everyone.

640
34:20.246 --> 34:23.249
Thank you all for coming today.

641
34:23.332 --> 34:25.418
I'm glad to see all of you!

642
34:31.007 --> 34:33.634
Now then, please give the closing statement.

643
34:34.969 --> 34:38.472
Making customers beautiful and seeing them leave with a smile.

644
34:39.056 --> 34:42.185
That is my goal in life.

645
34:44.437 --> 34:45.938
Thank you very much.

646
34:46.689 --> 34:48.024
For today only,

647
34:48.107 --> 34:51.277
those who purchase the Angewel Perfect Beauty Set

648
34:51.360 --> 34:55.198
will receive a free 2-month extension on their contract!

649
34:59.660 --> 35:00.536
Everyone!

650
35:01.037 --> 35:02.538
This salon is a scam.

651
35:02.622 --> 35:05.082
If you sign, they won't let you make reservations.

652
35:05.166 --> 35:06.334
Sir, please calm down.

653
35:06.417 --> 35:08.127
We have proof right here.

654
35:09.962 --> 35:11.923
This is not for the trial plan.

655
35:12.006 --> 35:14.717
I reserved spots for people who already signed with us.

656
35:14.800 --> 35:17.970
I told you to make reservations for the trial plan!

657
35:18.054 --> 35:20.264
Only first-time customers get reservations!

658
35:20.348 --> 35:23.976
-Only first-timers? -Now Ms. Katsuta will be mad at me!

659
35:24.852 --> 35:26.729
Why do they have this audio?

660
35:30.149 --> 35:31.567
It's a misunderstanding.

661
35:32.360 --> 35:36.447
Trial customers, and of course,

662
35:36.530 --> 35:39.784
contracted customers will receive their treatments too.

663
35:40.701 --> 35:42.161
May I add something?

664
35:42.245 --> 35:43.496
What is it?

665
35:43.579 --> 35:47.083
I'm a beauty geek, and I checked the serum used by the salon.

666
35:47.166 --> 35:49.877
The ingredients were different from off-the-shelf products.

667
35:51.128 --> 35:53.589
Of course, we use our own special formula.

668
35:53.673 --> 35:55.007
What I mean is,

669
35:55.091 --> 35:58.511
all the ingredients in their serum are present in very small amounts.

670
35:58.594 --> 36:00.596
-What? -Yes.

671
36:01.222 --> 36:05.476
I was thinking, maybe it's heavily diluted?

672
36:05.559 --> 36:06.769
Like this.

673
36:21.325 --> 36:23.327
Everyone, please don't be deceived.

674
36:23.411 --> 36:26.414
Both the photos and the audio are fake!

675
36:26.497 --> 36:30.626
You say that, but you fabricated contracts

676
36:30.710 --> 36:33.879
so people can't easily cancel, didn't you?

677
36:34.463 --> 36:36.215
What?

678
36:37.091 --> 36:38.384
When did you…

679
36:38.467 --> 36:40.177
They're lying!

680
36:40.261 --> 36:43.723
It's all just lies! None of it is true!

681
36:43.806 --> 36:45.933
You deceived us! Screw you!

682
36:51.731 --> 36:53.399
What is going on?

683
36:58.696 --> 37:01.115
You're the lawyer from before.

684
37:01.782 --> 37:03.409
Is this your doing?

685
37:03.492 --> 37:04.368
What?

686
37:04.910 --> 37:09.332
Eavesdropping, secretly taking photos! What you people did is a crime!

687
37:09.415 --> 37:10.374
I'll sue you!

688
37:13.794 --> 37:15.880
You are the one getting sued here.

689
37:16.797 --> 37:19.383
You rejected reservations after securing contracts

690
37:19.467 --> 37:22.636
and fabricated contracts so customers cannot cancel.

691
37:22.720 --> 37:25.264
We can get you for fraud and document falsification.

692
37:27.058 --> 37:30.853
I already found many others who suffered the same kind of damage.

693
37:30.936 --> 37:34.982
If you don't want us to take legal action, refund the money right now.

694
37:44.700 --> 37:46.285
Thank you very much.

695
37:47.203 --> 37:49.997
The salon has agreed to issue a full refund.

696
37:50.081 --> 37:52.583
It's all thanks to what you did, Ms. Aso.

697
37:53.167 --> 37:56.462
I'm so happy. Now you two can make up.

698
37:58.172 --> 38:00.466
I still intend to divorce him.

699
38:00.549 --> 38:01.717
What?

700
38:01.801 --> 38:03.511
Because of this incident,

701
38:03.594 --> 38:07.056
I can no longer talk and laugh with him like before.

702
38:07.139 --> 38:10.476
We've both come to lose trust in each other.

703
38:12.103 --> 38:15.523
Man, this house really is well-made.

704
38:15.606 --> 38:16.482
Mr. Uramawashi!

705
38:18.442 --> 38:19.360
Here.

706
38:19.985 --> 38:22.738
A scale model of your house.

707
38:22.822 --> 38:24.907
The interior looks like this.

708
38:26.033 --> 38:28.744
The inspiration for this house

709
38:28.828 --> 38:35.376
comes from Frank Lloyd Wright's Fallingwater Museum, completed in 1936.

710
38:35.459 --> 38:36.836
Do you know it?

711
38:37.503 --> 38:38.796
No.

712
38:39.630 --> 38:44.009
He and the house's owner were at odds, but they made many compromises

713
38:44.093 --> 38:46.011
and built the house together.

714
38:46.095 --> 38:47.179
Ultimately,

715
38:47.721 --> 38:51.976
it became a masterpiece worthy of becoming a World Heritage site.

716
38:53.686 --> 38:57.815
Don't you think building a house is similar to life?

717
38:58.899 --> 39:03.070
Environment, land, climate.

718
39:04.530 --> 39:06.365
And above all,

719
39:07.324 --> 39:12.538
the compromises you make with the person you live with.

720
39:15.040 --> 39:17.042
Also, the lighting.

721
39:17.918 --> 39:19.712
The lighting…

722
39:22.882 --> 39:26.302
Well, you're separating anyway. Guess we don't need to discuss it.

723
39:27.720 --> 39:28.637
Mr. Uramawashi!

724
39:30.973 --> 39:33.767
Well then, I'll leave the rest to you.

725
39:34.393 --> 39:35.478
Take care of it.

726
39:45.404 --> 39:46.739
If I recall correctly…

727
39:47.448 --> 39:49.450
Before deciding on this lighting,

728
39:50.284 --> 39:53.078
you two hesitated for two whole months, right?

729
39:54.663 --> 39:57.917
That's right. I said I wanted something showier.

730
39:58.626 --> 40:02.254
And I said, since it's the living room, let's keep it simple.

731
40:02.338 --> 40:06.050
When I thought about it carefully, I realized I preferred simple too.

732
40:06.884 --> 40:09.678
The wallpaper, the flooring, the doorknobs…

733
40:10.262 --> 40:13.432
For each of them, you two agonized, discussed,

734
40:13.516 --> 40:16.143
and made all these decisions together, right?

735
40:20.022 --> 40:23.108
But that was back then.

736
40:23.859 --> 40:26.070
Things are different now.

737
40:27.112 --> 40:29.031
I think it's still the same.

738
40:31.367 --> 40:32.618
I mean,

739
40:33.410 --> 40:36.580
you went to the salon because you wanted to be prettier

740
40:36.664 --> 40:38.374
for your husband, right?

741
40:38.457 --> 40:39.500
Huh?

742
40:40.501 --> 40:42.920
You still do things for each other's sake.

743
40:43.003 --> 40:45.589
I think it was all just a slight misunderstanding.

744
40:45.673 --> 40:46.840
Even so,

745
40:48.842 --> 40:50.678
it's too late to turn back now.

746
41:00.980 --> 41:06.193
Your husband said that without you, there's no point in living in that house.

747
41:06.277 --> 41:07.111
Huh?

748
41:07.194 --> 41:08.195
Huh?

749
41:08.279 --> 41:09.947
He told me that the other day.

750
41:10.990 --> 41:12.408
Didn't you?

751
41:19.957 --> 41:21.250
Yes.

752
41:25.629 --> 41:28.090
We built it for the two of us to live in.

753
41:30.050 --> 41:33.178
If we don't live in it together, it's pointless.

754
41:39.518 --> 41:43.731
Personally, I don't know anything about architecture,

755
41:44.690 --> 41:46.483
but I feel like this house

756
41:46.567 --> 41:50.070
will become a place packed with both of your hopes.

757
41:57.286 --> 42:00.873
I said so many terrible things. I'm sorry.

758
42:01.582 --> 42:03.542
I'm sorry too.

759
42:05.836 --> 42:06.920
I…

760
42:07.713 --> 42:12.593
want to finish this house and live in it with you.

761
42:14.511 --> 42:16.639
Yeah. Me too.

762
42:18.974 --> 42:22.770
Man, I was worried about what would happen with the house.

763
42:22.853 --> 42:24.271
It's really nice.

764
42:24.355 --> 42:25.397
Yeah.

765
42:25.481 --> 42:28.150
-So detailed! It even has stairs. -Does it?

766
42:34.031 --> 42:36.825
This time, I made zero mistakes.

767
42:36.909 --> 42:39.078
Because you had the easiest role.

768
42:39.161 --> 42:40.829
With all due respect…

769
42:40.913 --> 42:42.623
I bought drinks.

770
42:42.706 --> 42:43.957
Thank you.

771
42:44.041 --> 42:47.836
There's no such thing as an easy role! Here you go.

772
42:47.920 --> 42:50.506
I'm glad the Takashimas were able to make up.

773
42:50.589 --> 42:53.258
A house like that needs a loving couple living in it!

774
42:53.342 --> 42:58.597
Building houses is a tough job, but it can change people's lives too.

775
42:58.681 --> 43:00.557
Don't you think it's worth doing?

776
43:00.641 --> 43:03.352
Nakazaki, why don't you become an architect too?

777
43:03.435 --> 43:04.561
Yes, I will.

778
43:04.645 --> 43:05.646
-Come again? -Seriously?

779
43:05.729 --> 43:07.731
Actually, I've already been studying.

780
43:08.732 --> 43:11.068
I bet you did it because you admired me.

781
43:11.151 --> 43:12.611
No, it has to be me!

782
43:12.695 --> 43:14.947
You're an assistant! No way he admires you.

783
43:15.030 --> 43:17.908
The First-Class Architect preliminary exam… I passed it.

784
43:17.991 --> 43:19.868
Whoa, congrats!

785
43:20.411 --> 43:21.829
Fail the next part.

786
43:21.912 --> 43:23.288
-Fail… -You're terrible!

787
43:23.372 --> 43:24.623
When did Mr. Takashima

788
43:24.707 --> 43:27.835
say there is no point living in a house without her?

789
43:27.918 --> 43:30.462
Thanks to that, they were able to make up.

790
43:31.255 --> 43:32.756
Actually, that was…

791
43:32.840 --> 43:34.174
a lie.

792
43:34.258 --> 43:35.092
Huh?

793
43:35.175 --> 43:37.636
I really wanted them to reconcile.

794
43:37.720 --> 43:41.014
So, I blurted it out, and the husband played along.

795
43:41.098 --> 43:42.516
It was a lie to you,

796
43:42.599 --> 43:45.227
but the husband actually felt that way too.

797
43:45.310 --> 43:48.021
Both of them were looking for a chance to make up.

798
43:49.356 --> 43:50.566
Right?

799
43:53.318 --> 43:54.653
You pass.

800
43:57.072 --> 44:00.743
A lawyer has got to be able to tell a lie or two!

801
44:01.326 --> 44:03.954
Wait, so you were testing me?

802
44:04.037 --> 44:05.998
You did splendidly.

803
44:06.081 --> 44:08.667
Unbelievable. You're absurd.

804
44:10.669 --> 44:11.837
Aso.

805
44:13.255 --> 44:17.468
You've become a better lawyer than before.

806
44:19.344 --> 44:21.346
Thanks to me.

807
44:22.598 --> 44:24.308
That's not true!

808
44:24.391 --> 44:26.894
I grew through my own efforts!

809
44:26.977 --> 44:31.648
Well then, now that you've grown, Ms. Aso, please be our retained counsel!

810
44:31.732 --> 44:33.275
I don't want to.

811
44:33.358 --> 44:36.653
You say that, but you'll take the job anyway.

812
44:36.737 --> 44:38.155
I won't do it.

813
44:38.238 --> 44:39.698
Ms. Aso!

814
44:40.741 --> 44:42.868
Do you want to have lunch with me sometime?

815
44:43.952 --> 44:46.330
I guess tea would be fine.

816
44:46.413 --> 44:47.414
-What? -Huh?

817
44:47.498 --> 44:48.624
Are you sure?

818
44:48.707 --> 44:49.917
Awesome!

819
44:50.709 --> 44:52.252
She's lying again, right?

820
44:52.336 --> 44:54.254
Who knows? She has grown, after all.

821
44:56.131 --> 44:57.382
Well then.

822
44:57.466 --> 44:59.676
I'll be taking my leave.

823
44:59.760 --> 45:01.261
For work?

824
45:02.638 --> 45:05.349
I'm busy with my lawyer work.

825
45:05.432 --> 45:06.558
Lawyer…

826
45:06.642 --> 45:09.061
Didn't you quit?

827
45:09.603 --> 45:11.063
That was…

828
45:11.146 --> 45:13.148
CLOSED FOR BUSINESS

829
45:13.232 --> 45:14.733
…a lie.

830
45:15.567 --> 45:16.777
What?!

831
45:22.157 --> 45:23.742
Right, Ms. Aso.

832
45:23.825 --> 45:24.826
Have a seat.

833
45:24.910 --> 45:27.287
-Oh, right. -Come on, eat with us.

834
45:27.371 --> 45:28.205
Thank you.

835
45:28.288 --> 45:30.207
-Here. -Thank you.

836
45:30.791 --> 45:31.959
Want a drink?

837
45:32.042 --> 45:33.794
-We have beer! -Beer, please.

838
45:33.877 --> 45:35.796
-I want a beer. -Want some pizza?

839
45:35.879 --> 45:37.130
-Sure. -Which one?

840
45:37.214 --> 45:38.173
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
